I haven't seen this brought up in a while, and it's something that
still bothers me.

NH seems to arbitrarily treat "Chaotic" as "Evil" or "Not Evil".
Chaotics can murder and sacrafice their own species; these are
generally considered "evil" things.  However, Elves are Chaotic; Elves
are generally considered "not evil"*.

At the risk of making NH more similar to D&D, why not implement a more
cohesive alignment-system - so that Elves, while carefree and Chaotic,
are restricted from doing specifically Evil things such as murder?  I
think that making Elves Neutral would be unbalancing, in terms of
making one of the most useful races also capable of getting some of the
best artifacts, but I just don't like that such a noble race is allowed
to do such heinous things.



* Unless NH elves are supposed to be drawn from Pratchett's "Lords and
Ladies".



